{
  "name": "works-geoscience",
  "title": "Geoscience",
  "base": "works-core",
  "description": "The lean shell plus the geoscience/tabular Data Workbench (CSV / OMF block models, grade-tonnage, swath).",
  "packages": ["@gcu/notebook", "@gcu/workbench"],
  "settings": { "appearance": { "theme": "dark" } },
  "welcome": [
    { "kind": "notebook" },
    { "kind": "doc", "content": "# Welcome to Auditable Works — Geoscience\n\nThis workstation has the **Data Workbench** installed: open **Tools → Data workbench**, point it at a CSV or OMF block model, and it streams **schema · summary stats · grade-tonnage · swath · categories** without loading the file into memory.\n\nOther places to poke:\n\n- **Tools → Terminal** — a real shell (geas): `ls /`, `pkg search`, `profile current`.\n- **Tools → Library** — browse and install content packs and extensions.\n- **Tools → Set up / change profile…** — re-provision or add packages any time.\n\nThis profile also ships an **interactive tour notebook** (it generates a synthetic block model to explore) — it appears once a notebook surface is available in this shell. Delete this file whenever you're done with it." }
  ],
  "starter": [
    { "type": "md", "code": "# Welcome to Auditable Works — Geoscience\n\nThis workstation has the **Data Workbench** installed: point it at a CSV or OMF block model and it streams **schema · summary stats · grade-tonnage · swath · categories** without loading the file into memory.\n\nThere's no sample data yet — the cell below **generates** a small synthetic block model (so this profile stays a few hundred bytes). Run it (▶ on the cell, or Run all in the toolbar):" },
    { "type": "code", "code": "// A synthetic porphyry-ish block model — a grade shell around a core,\n// written as a data sibling of this notebook so the Data Workbench can scan it.\nconst rng = ((s) => () => (s = (s * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0) / 2 ** 32)(42);\nconst rows = ['x,y,z,cu,au,domain'];\nfor (let i = 0; i < 4000; i++) {\n  const x = 10 * Math.floor(rng() * 60), y = 10 * Math.floor(rng() * 60), z = 10 * Math.floor(rng() * 30);\n  const d = Math.hypot(x - 300, y - 300, (z - 150) * 2);\n  const shell = Math.exp(-d / 220);\n  const cu = +(shell * (0.2 + 1.4 * rng())).toFixed(3);\n  const au = +(shell * (0.05 + 0.6 * rng())).toFixed(3);\n  rows.push(`${x},${y},${z},${cu},${au},${d < 180 ? 'core' : 'halo'}`);\n}\nawait notebook.fs.writeFile('blockmodel.csv', rows.join('\\n'));\nprint(`wrote blockmodel.csv — ${rows.length - 1} blocks`);" },
    { "type": "md", "code": "Now open **Tools → Data workbench** and point it at:\n\n```\n/projects/welcome/blockmodel.csv\n```\n\nTry **Summary stats** on `cu`, **Grade-tonnage** (the core/halo domains give it shape), and a **Swath** along x.\n\nOther places to poke: **Tools → Terminal** is a real shell (`ls /`, `pkg search`, `profile current`); **Tools → Library** browses installable content and extensions; **File → New notebook** starts your own. Re-provision or add packages any time from **Tools → Set up / change profile…** — and delete this notebook whenever you're done with it." }
  ]
}
